# Secrets and authenticated state: never in version control (ARCHITECTURE.md, Storage and
# configuration). The browser storage_state is a live Principle session, not just a cookie.
.env
*.storage_state.json
config.local.toml

# Runtime data lives outside the checkout on a real host; these are the dev-machine copies.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
logs/
run/
# Production reads and proofs made from them: real patient records.
prod_data/
# Chromium's crash reporter writes this into the working directory under Playwright.
debug.log

# Anything captured from staging before scrubbing. Recordings enter the repo only via
# scripts/record_principle_wire.py, which scrubs at capture.
*.raw.json
screenshots/
*.png

.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Recordings captured from a real Principle tenant are NOT distributed. They are derived from
# real patient records, and no anonymiser should be trusted enough to publish its output under
# health-privacy law. Each practice runs scripts/record_principle_wire.py against its own
# staging tenant and keeps the result locally.
#
# Refusal recordings ARE committed: an error body is the API's own wording and carries no
# patient data, and tests/fake/server.py needs them to refuse in words nobody invented.
tests/recordings/*.json
tests/recordings/firestore/
!tests/recordings/refusals/

# Principle's published specification is fetched, never committed: it carries no licence, no
# terms and no contact, so redistribution rights are unstated, and it cannot be sublicensed
# under this project's AGPL-3.0. tests/spec/fingerprint.json is the derived description we do
# commit (scripts/refresh_spec.py).
tests/spec/principle-api.yml
